          "question": "my poo has been really dark, almost black and sticky, for three days and I feel light headed when i stand",
          "answer": "**Please seek medical care today, and go to an emergency department now if you feel faint, have a racing heartbeat, become short of breath, or pass more dark or bloody stool.** Black, sticky stool together with feeling light-headed when you stand needs prompt in-person assessment. The automated check returned a \"routine\" label, but it matched no listed pattern, and the tool itself says that is not a clearance.\n\nThe guidance on gastrointestinal bleeding (educational summary, \"Gastrointestinal bleeding\") says that black, tarry stool can come from bleeding higher up in the digestive tract. It also says this kind of bleeding often involves more blood loss than the stool's appearance suggests. The document recommends assuming bleeding until a clinician has assessed it. Iron supplements and some medicines can also darken stool, but the same document warns against assuming that is the cause without checking.\n\nThe guidance on stomach reflux (GERD, \"Alarm features that change the approach\") lists black tarry stools as a reason for prompt endoscopy, a test that looks inside the digestive tract. The retrieved passages do not cover dizziness on standing, so I can't tell you what that symptom means on its own. Please mention it to the clinician.\n\nCall emergency services or go to the nearest emergency department if you feel faint or collapse, your heartbeat is racing or pounding, you feel short of breath, or you vomit blood or material that looks like coffee grounds. Do not wait for a routine appointment.\n\n*Not medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.*",
